        "content": "<p>alexcrichton <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15216#issuecomment-6773584992\">commented</a> on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/15216\">issue #15216</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is actually a Rust miscomiple we're affected by. The fix is to update our Rust toolchain used, such as <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15218\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15218</a>. That'll eventually percolate to a new release which means wasmtime-py will get fixed. In the meantime I'd recommend skipping wasmtime-py 50</p>\n</blockquote>",
